            <ArticleTitle>A novel BBS10 mutation identified in a patient with Bardet-Biedl syndrome with a violent emotional outbreak.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17033</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/hgv.2017.33</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 10-year-old girl with Bardet-Biedl syndrome caused by a novel mutation in the Bardet-Biedl syndrome 10 (BBS10) gene. She had multiple malformations, including a dysmorphic face, postaxial polydactyly, polycystic kidney and amblyopia. She presented with typical BBS features, including intellectual disability with emotional outbursts and mild obesity. Whole-exome sequencing identified compound heterozygous mutations with NM_024685.3:c.1677C&gt;A [p.(Tyr559*)] and c.1974T&gt;G [p.(Tyr658*)]. To our knowledge, the latter mutation has never been reported previously.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
